Gaspode wrote:
>
> Last night while playing I accidently stumbled upon a hidden stash on a
> level and at first I wasn't quite sure what had happened.  Apparently I
> had found a 1x1 room

Looks like you're new so I'll review common terminology in RGRN.
The one-square rooms are called closets.

> and while searching I was teleported to the stash.

Here a stash is a place you drop a lot of your stuff.  Those 2x2
rooms are called vaults or MMVs (Magic Money Vaults).

>  I picked up all of the gold, and then a guard appeared and told me to
> leave the money and then follow him out.  Besides teleportation is
> there a way to get out.

Following his instructions works really well.  He will lead you to
an open part of the level (corridor or room) and disappear.  But
you will still know where the vault is.  Digging is not a problem
once you've learned at least one of the ways how.

> It seems that killing the guard may be a bad
> idea as he leads you out.

Punishment includes one point of lost luck, lost telepathy, and
guards are mean enough that low level players often can't survive
the battle.  In exchange there's an infinite supply of guards and
they leave armor.  Trouble is, by the time you can easily kill one
vault guard after another chances are you already have better
armor than they leave.

> Is this why you see the "You hear a guard
> muttering" message?

If a level has a vault there are several possible messages that
can happen.  Play close attention to such messages as they
will tell you about the level you're on.  You definitely want to
know if there's a vault or fountain or courtroom or whatever on
your level.

> Are these 1x1 rooms that seem to appear fairly
> often used for anything else?

There are several possible types of traps.  You've only found the
1-time teleportation trap type so far I suspect.  Also they don't
always have a secret door.  A non-secret door is okay but no
door at all makes them much harder to find.  And sometimes
they have items in them.



